{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And if a lamb, etc., through and it shall be forgiven him.</b> One needs to know why it was necessary to divide them into two sections, for it should have said above ״and he shall bring his offering, a female goat, etc., or a female lamb, without blemish״ and so on, and it would not have been necessary to write the entire section. It appears that the verse divided them for its own reason, which our Rabbis of blessed memory stated (Torat Kohanim 3) in the section of וְאִם עֵז — that it comes to include the fat-tail (alyah) in a sin-offering from the flock. Therefore it carefully specified regarding the lamb ״כַּאֲשֶׁר יוּרַם חֵלֶב הַכֶּשֶׂב,״ and regarding the goat it said ״וְאֶת כָּל חֶלְבָּהּ יָסִיר״ — one matter for peace/freewill offerings and one matter for obligatory sin-offerings." "It also appears to me that there is a novelty in everything stated here. Its saying <b>and he shall lay [his hand]</b> — our Rabbis of blessed memory derived (Torat Kohanim here) that it comes to teach about the sin-offering of a nazirite and the sin-offering of a metzora, which require semichah. And its saying <b>and he shall slaughter it for a sin-offering</b> — they derived (Zevachim 7a) that the slaughter must be for the sake of a sin-offering, and this detail was not alluded to in the section of the goat, and from here you learn for both of them. And its saying <b>in the place where</b> etc. — they said in Zevachim (Zevachim 48b) in the chapter אֵיזֶהוּ מְקוֹמָן: From where do we know that the sin-offering requires the north? As it is written ״וְשָׁחַט הַחַטָּאת בִּמְקוֹם הָעוֹלָה״ — we have found it as a mitzvah; from where [do we know it is required] לְעִכּוּבָא (as a binding requirement)? As it is written ״בִּמְקוֹם אֲשֶׁר יִשְׁחַט אֶת הָעוֹלָה״ etc. — until here. See that two verses were required. And there in the Talmud it raised the point that this teaches for all sin-offerings as a mitzvah. And its saying (Torat Kohanim here) <b>of the blood of the sin-offering</b> — they derived that one must receive its blood for the sake of a sin-offering, and so too in everything that is repeated there is a novel halachic point, and therefore Scripture divided them to teach statutes and judgments, etc."], :book :leviticus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:53:17.739364544Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}